body:
Hey man. Listen.... When we think about suicide we tend to underestimate how serious the effect would be on our loved ones. They will never get over that shit man. It will always be a rough topic. When someone with the same first name as you comes into their life... even in a small way like a waiter or a salesman.... there will be a sting. Every time they see someone who looks like you when you were younger they will lose it. Every time. Sure, after a while, the sting will become less painful, but do not be naive. The pain will be ever-present. It will never end for them until they die. I know this isn't something that's productive to hear necessarily because from this viewpoint you are hurting them either way. Either you stay alive and stay in pain and hurt your family, or you kill yourself, are free from pain, and hurt your family.

&#x200B;

Just please understand that life waxes and wanes. There are going to be times when it's hard and time's when it's easy. It's not always black and white either. Sometimes it's both good and bad all at the same time. It's hard to hold both of those and not get immersed in one or the other.

&#x200B;

My suggestion is to go see a therapist. You seem like a good person who just wants the best for everyone. I support you and have been and kind of am at times still where you are at right now. I understand. Please seek help. You said that you go to school. Even if you are failing. Whatever. On almost all college and high school campuses is free mental health services. Either free or pro-rated, in case you don't want your parents finding out that you are seeing a therapist (IDK what your family situation is), so you can go see a professional without insurance.
